+/**
+ * tcg_region_fork_start, tcg_region_fork_end: Keep a split JIT private
+ *
+ * A split rw/rx JIT buffer is one shared memory object mapped twice.  A
+ * process created by fork() would keep sharing it with its parent, and
+ * each would overwrite the other's translations.  With every vCPU stopped,
+ * tcg_region_fork_start() copies the used part of the buffer into a new
+ * object; in the child, tcg_region_fork_end() maps that copy over both
+ * views at their existing addresses.  Both do nothing for a buffer that
+ * is not split.
+ */
+void tcg_region_fork_start(void);
+void tcg_region_fork_end(bool child);
